# Xcode and Simulator: MCP only

**Scope:** Binding only when `dev-ios-scope.mdc` marks this workspace active (iOS Simulator workflow). When inactive, ignore this entire rule — use Shell `xcodebuild` or **`xcode-tools`** on macOS.

Build, test, launch, boot, and shutdown on **Simulator** go through `XcodeBuildMCP` or **`xcode-tools`** (in-window). **`xcode-tools`** also applies to macOS targets when Xcode is open; this rule’s Shell ban applies only while dev-ios-scope is **active**. Do not use the Shell tool (or any other non-MCP tool) for those operations.

Never run, chain, or wrap any of these in Shell, including after `pkill`, `kill`, `nohup`, or `sleep`:

- `xcodebuild` (including `test-without-building`)
- `xcrun`, `simctl`, `xcode-select`
- `instruments`, `xed`, `agvtool`, `ibtool`, `actool`

**Reading logs and crashes is allowed.** Use Read, Grep, or Glob on runtime console logs, crash reports, and Diagnostics for the host app on Simulator or device, including paths under `~/Library/Logs/` (for example `CoreSimulator`, `DiagnosticReports`), `~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/…/data/Library/Logs/`, and log file paths returned by MCP (`build_run_sim`, `test_sim`, `GetBuildLog`). `debug_attach_sim` does not replace those for a crash that already happened; read the on-disk logs when investigating a prior crash.

Do not **write** or **delete** under `DerivedData`, `SourcePackages`, `CoreSimulator`, `~/Library/Developer/Xcode`, `~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator`, or `/Applications/Xcode.app` unless the user explicitly asks. Do not `kill` / `pkill` `xcodebuild` PIDs from hygiene `status`.

Hooks in this plugin run only from the Cursor plugin copy (`hooks/deny-xcode-bypass.sh`), never from the repository tree.

If MCP is unavailable, stop and report that. Do not fall back to Shell for build, test, launch, boot, or shutdown. The only Shell exceptions are bundled scripts under `plugins/dev-ios/skills/*/scripts/` when the matching skill is loaded and instructs that script — in particular `resolve-derived-data-path.sh` from `build-ios-apps` and `simulator-hygiene.sh` from `ios-simulator-browser`.
